{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction","kind":"proposition","title":"The far-commuting slots cannot carry $\\mathrm{SU}(2)_L$: non-abelianness is localized to the inter-slot linking","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-hoefsmit-ew-cell-content","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-ew-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution"],"tags":["electroweak","su2","far-commutation","obstruction","non-abelian","categorical-linking","weak-sector"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.ParticleInteractions.su2L_nonabelianness_not_in_slots","text":"ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction.md","leanSource":"ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction\"></a><p>*Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> be a ring. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_1, \\sigma_3, \\sigma_5 \\in A</code> be the braid generators hosting the electroweak carriers on the disjoint strand-pairs, subject to the braid far-commutation relation</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\sigma_i \\sigma_j = \\sigma_j \\sigma_i \\qquad (|i - j| \\ge 2),</code></pre>\n<p>and let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{A}_{\\mathrm{slot}} \\subseteq A</code> be the subalgebra they generate. Suppose <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">J_1, J_2, J_3 \\in A</code> realise an <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{su}(2)_L</code> adjoint structure relation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[J_1, J_2] = J_3</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">J_3 \\ne 0</code>. Then <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">J_1</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">J_2</code> cannot both lie in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{A}_{\\mathrm{slot}}</code>: the non-abelian <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{SU}(2)_L</code> structure cannot be realised purely among the far-commuting slots.*</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"9.8.10","page":"b/prop-ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction","qa":{"counts":{"pass":77,"fail":1,"warn":1,"na":13,"unknown":0,"stale":63},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.ParticleInteractions.su2L_nonabelianness_not_in_slots","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
